    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113318" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χανδόν</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with mouth wide open,
				greedily, eagerly,</i> [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶνον] χ. ἑλεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.294
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.</u>
				1.1.11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				341
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				4.430
			</span></i> (cj.), etc.; in late Prose <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ.
				ἐκπιεῖν, πιέσθαι, πίνειν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.735
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Merc. Cond.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Mis.</u>
				338c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					71.10
				</span></i>
			; metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἐνεπίμπλαντο εὐχῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Alex.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἐμπιπλάμενος τοῦ ὕπνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Im.</u>
					2.22
				</span></i>
			.</div>
